{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chuanle song\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -LiteralPath 'pipeline/designs/exp_design_20260924-150200.md' -Raw\"","aggregated_output":"# Experiment Design - AdaRES_project\n\n2026-09-24 15:02 Asia/Shanghai\n\n## 1. Motivation\nGoal: improve the 3D-RES learned-indicator baseline to ScanRefer mIoU >=\n0.515. Active capacity is 1/2; candidate budget 1. F4 tests whether\nprevious-layer mask geometry can redirect decoder evidence retrieval.\n\n## 2. Current Best Results\n| ID | State | Best mIoU | Epochs |\n|---|---|---:|---:|\n| B1 | completed | 0.5020 | baseline |\n| B4-E30 | completed champion | 0.5094 | 30 |\n| C1-E30 / C2-E30 | completed | 0.5008 / 0.5014 | 30 |\n| D1 | running GPU0 | pending | 30 planned |\n\n## 3. Analysis & Direction\nB4's competition indicator improved B1 by 0.0074 but remains 0.0056\nbelow target. F1/F2/F3 confidence proxies were contradicted by bounded\ndiagnoses. F4 modifies spatial information flow in the decoder, independent\nof D1's full-query confidence comparison. The positive predicted-foreground\ncoverage proxy is not a demonstrated effect on segmentation IoU.\n\n## 4. Experiment Plan\n| ID | Config | Structural hypothesis | Control | Success criterion |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| AdaRES-F4 | configs_song/model_paper5/adares_f4_mask_reanchor_res.yaml | Reanchor layer i>0 fine/query attention using previous mask soft centroid | B4-E30, same fresh 30-epoch protocol | mIoU > 0.5094; target 0.5150 |\n\nFor valid superpoints v, query q and previous layer i-1:\n\n```\np(q,v) = sigmoid(mask_logit(i-1,q,v)) * valid(v)\nc(i,q) = sum_v p(q,v) * xyz(v) / max(sum_v p(q,v), eps)\na(i,q) = c(i,q) if any valid mask_logit(i-1,q,v)>0 else seed_xyz(q)\nN(i,q) = topk_nearest(a(i,q), fine_xyz, k_i)\n```\n\nAt i=0 use seed_xyz. The center calculation is stop-gradient; task-loss\ngradients still reach the decoder through sampled attention values and all\noriginal paths. No oracle masks or labels enter the anchor.\n\n## 5. GPU Allocation Plan\n| Server | GPU | Assignment |\n|---|---:|---|\n| server-2 | 0 | Continue D1, untouched |\n| server-2 | 1 | F4 only if all six admission gates pass |\n| server-6 | any | Prohibited |\n\n## 6. Implementation Checklist\n- [x] Independent model package and unique YAML; B4 YAML parity.\n- [x] Static syntax and architectural diff.\n- [ ] Native real training batch forward/backward and anchor edge tests.\n- [ ] Matched B4 batch resource control; avoid OOM/foreign processes.\n- [ ] Six-gate review, hashed admission receipt and candidate-only commit.\n- [ ] Verified additive sync, gated queue dispatch, unique PID and increasing Train[1/30] steps.\n\n## 7. Risk Assessment\nThe centroid can lock onto wrong foreground, and soft low-confidence\nbackground can bias it. Proxy coverage is measured against predictions;\nit does not prove better ground truth coverage. Monitor gradient finiteness,\nGPU1 memory, and step progress. If native tests fail, do not enqueue.\nIf trained F4 underperforms, close it without validation-driven re-tuning.\n\nStatus: VALIDATION PENDING. No admission or training asserted.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chuanle song\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -LiteralPath 'pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-F4_reanchor_diagnosis_20260924-150200.md' -Raw\"","aggregated_output":"# AdaRES-F4 decoder neighborhood diagnosis\n\n2026-09-24 15:02 Asia/Shanghai. Fixed B4-E30 best checkpoint, first 16\nScanRefer validation scenes (441 expressions), read-only server-2 GPU1 probe.\nThe F4 intervention is decoder neighborhood reanchoring, not an inference-time\nconfidence reranker.\n\nThe B4 decoder anchors its local fine cross-attention and query self-attention\nto immutable sampled seed positions. The probe compared four nearest valid\nsuperpoints around each seed and around the previous predicted-mask soft\ncentroid against **final predicted foreground** for the missed oracle query.\nAmong 240 material selection errors, 113 center neighborhoods covered more\nof that foreground, 16 covered less; average proxy coverage was 0.14642\n(seed) versus 0.23379 (center). There is room for an information-flow\nintervention, not evidence of improved trained mIoU.\n\nLimitations: the oracle is chosen with ground truth only for diagnosis, never\nat inference. The probe uses all valid superpoints, whereas actual fine\ncross-attention selects up to 512 via coarse attention; the query self-attention\nalso uses a separate top-k mask. It measures overlap with **predicted** final\nforeground, not ground-truth foreground, so high coverage may reinforce a\nwrong prediction. It is observational, from one trained checkpoint and 16\nvalidation scenes. No causal or population claim follows.\n\nThe proposed test changes the attention neighborhood anchor after the initial\ndecoder layer. It retains B4's scoring indicator, query sampling, top-k sizes,\ntraining loss, seed and 30-epoch schedule. Empty predicted foreground uses\nthe original seed; padded superpoints are excluded. Training from the\nreleased SPFormer backbone, compare with the B4-E30 protocol control.\n\nEvidence: `pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-F4_reanchor_16scenes_20260924.json`\nand `AdaRES/tools/diagnose_adares_f4_reanchor.py`.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chuanle song\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -LiteralPath 'AdaRES/tools/diagnose_adares_b4_selection.py' -TotalCount 240\"","aggregated_output":"import argparse\r\nimport json\r\nimport statistics\r\nimport sys\r\nimport types\r\nfrom pathlib import Path\r\n\r\nimport gorilla\r\nimport torch\r\nimport torch.nn.functional as F\r\n\r\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\r\nsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT))\r\n\r\nfrom ipdn.dataset import build_dataset\r\nfrom ipdn.model_paper5.adares_b4_query_competition import IPDN\r\nfrom ipdn.utils import get_root_logger\r\n\r\n\r\ndef selection_predictor():\r\n    def predict_by_feat(\r\n        self, scan_ids, object_idss, ann_ids, out, superpoints,\r\n        gt_pmasks, gt_spmasks, fps_seed_sp,\r\n    ):\r\n        rows = []\r\n        for index, target in enumerate(gt_pmasks):\r\n            masks = out[\"masks\"][index].sigmoid().gt(0.5)\r\n            scores = F.softmax(out[\"indis\"][index], dim=-1)[:, 1]\r\n            selected = int(scores.argmax())\r\n            point_masks = masks[:, superpoints]\r\n            truth = target.gt(0.5).to(point_masks.device)\r\n            intersection = (point_masks & truth).sum(-1).float()\r\n            union = (point_masks | truth).sum(-1).float()\r\n            ious = intersection / union.clamp_min(1)\r\n            oracle = int(ious.argmax())\r\n            pair_intersection = (masks[selected] & masks[oracle]).sum().float()\r\n            pair_union = (masks[selected] | masks[oracle]).sum().float()\r\n            rows.append({\r\n                \"selected_iou\": float(ious[selected]),\r\n                \"oracle_iou\": float(ious[oracle]),\r\n                \"selected_oracle_overlap\": float(\r\n                    pair_intersection / pair_union.clamp_min(1)\r\n                ),\r\n                \"oracle_score_rank\": int(\r\n                    (scores.argsort(descending=True) == oracle)\r\n                    .nonzero(as_tuple=True)[0].item()\r\n                ) + 1,\r\n                \"selected_query\": selected,\r\n                \"oracle_query\": oracle,\r\n            })\r\n        return {\"rows\": rows}\r\n\r\n    return predict_by_feat\r\n\r\n\r\ndef main():\r\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\r\n    parser.add_argument(\"config\")\r\n    parser.add_argument(\"checkpoint\")\r\n    parser.add_argument(\"--output\", required=True)\r\n    parser.add_argument(\"--scenes\", type=int, default=16)\r\n    parser.add_argument(\"--gpu-id\", type=int, default=1)\r\n    args = parser.parse_args()\r\n\r\n    gorilla.set_cuda_visible_devices([args.gpu_id], 1)\r\n    gorilla.set_random_seed(1999)\r\n    cfg = gorilla.Config.fromfile(args.config)\r\n    data_cfg = cfg.data.val.copy()\r\n    data_cfg.training = False\r\n    data_cfg.aug = False\r\n    data_cfg.with_elastic = False\r\n    data_cfg.lang_num_max = 32\r\n    logger = get_root_logger()\r\n    dataset = build_dataset(data_cfg, logger)\r\n    model = IPDN(**cfg.model).cuda()\r\n    model.eval()\r\n    checkpoint = torch.load(args.checkpoint, map_location=\"cpu\")\r\n    state = checkpoint.get(\"model\", checkpoint)\r\n    if loaded.missing_keys or set(loaded.unexpected_keys) - allowed:\r\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"Checkpoint mismatch: {loaded}\")\r\n    model.predict_by_feat = types.MethodType(selection_predictor(), model)\r\n\r\n    rows = []\r\n    for index in range(min(args.scenes, len(dataset))):\r\n        batch = dataset.collate_fn([dataset[index]])\r\n        with torch.no_grad():\r\n            rows.extend(model(batch, mode=\"predict\")[\"rows\"])\r\n    if not rows:\r\n        raise RuntimeError(\"No expressions in diagnostic subset\")\r\n    errors = [row for row in rows if row[\"oracle_iou\"] - row[\"selected_iou\"] > 0.05]\r\n    result = {\r\n        \"checkpoint\": args.checkpoint,\r\n        \"scenes\": min(args.scenes, len(dataset)),\r\n        \"expressions\": len(rows),\r\n        \"top1_miou\": statistics.fmean(row[\"selected_iou\"] for row in rows),\r\n        \"oracle_miou\": statistics.fmean(row[\"oracle_iou\"] for row in rows),\r\n        \"material_error_count\": len(errors),\r\n        \"error_pair_overlap_mean\": (\r\n            statistics.fmean(row[\"selected_oracle_overlap\"] for row in errors)\r\n            if errors else None\r\n        ),\r\n        \"error_pair_overlap_ge_half\": sum(\r\n            row[\"selected_oracle_overlap\"] >= 0.5 for row in errors\r\n        ),\r\n        \"error_oracle_rank_le_three\": sum(\r\n            row[\"oracle_score_rank\"] <= 3 for row in errors\r\n        ),\r\n        \"rows\": rows,\r\n    }\r\n    Path(args.output).write_text(json.dumps(result, indent=2), encoding=\"utf-8\")\r\n    print(json.dumps({key: value for key, value in result.items() if key != \"rows\"}))\r\n\r\n\r\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\r\n    main()\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chuanle song\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -LiteralPath 'pipeline/reviews/motivation_review_20260924-150200.md' -Raw\"","aggregated_output":"# Motivation Review - AdaRES_project\n\n2026-09-24 15:02 Asia/Shanghai\n\n## 1. Goal\nThe goal is ScanRefer mIoU >= 0.5150, from a faithful learned-indicator\nbaseline. B1 is 0.5020; B4-E30 is 0.5094 (gap 0.0056). Allowed GPUs are\nserver-2 0/1, one experiment per GPU. New runs use fresh 30 epochs from the\nreleased SPFormer sparse-UNet backbone. No validation hyperparameter search.\nReport mIoU, Acc@0.25, Acc@0.5, active queries, latency and peak memory.\nSee `pipeline/goal.json` for the complete hard constraints and bans.\n\n## 2. Story Status\n| Hypothesis | Status | Evidence | Gap |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Query competition improves confidence | Supported | B4-E30 0.5094 | Causal isolation |\n| Full-query pair evidence improves selection | Running | D1 on GPU0 | Trained result |\n| Mask entropy, compactness and seed alignment rerank misses | Rejected | F1/F2/F3 bounded diagnoses | No tuning on validation |\n| Updated decoder neighborhoods improve target evidence | Proxy only | F4 113 better / 16 worse | Native intervention and training |\n\n## 3. Experiment Assessment\n| Experiment | mIoU | Contribution |\n|---|---:|---|\n| B1 | 0.5020 | Learned-indicator baseline |\n| B4-E30 | 0.5094 | Strongest matched-budget protocol control |\n| C1-E30/C2-E30 | 0.5008/0.5014 | Ranking losses failed to improve |\n| D1 | pending | All-query confidence modeling, distinct from F4 |\n| F1/F2/F3 | no training | Predicted diagnostic directions disconfirmed |\n\n## 4. Gap Analysis\nF4's 16-scene diagnostic finds that fixed seed neighborhoods often cover\nless final predicted foreground for missed-oracle queries. It does not test\ncausality, real fine-attention sampling or ground-truth foreground coverage.\nWhether reanchoring helps after fresh training is unknown.\n\n## 5. Design Rationale\nF4 modifies decoder information access, whereas D1 modifies the confidence\nindicator. With B4's top-k budget held fixed, a previous-layer mask provides\na causal candidate for where the next layer should gather spatial evidence.\nThe direction was fixed before training; neither threshold nor weight is\nselected on validation.\n\n## 6. Next Batch\nAdmit at most one F4 run on GPU1 after native backward, matched-B4 resource\ncontrol and all six gate proofs. If these fail, retain the stable F4 ID in\nresearch work with the exact failure; do not occupy the GPU for its own sake.\nSee `pipeline/designs/exp_design_20260924-150200.md`.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chuanle song\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -LiteralPath 'AdaRES/ipdn/model_paper5/adares_b4_query_competition/dec.py' -TotalCount 300\"","aggregated_output":"import torch\r\nimport torch.nn as nn\r\nfrom .sample_model import SamplingModule\r\nimport ipdn.torch.nn_new.functional as F\r\nfrom ipdn.torch.nn_new import MultiheadAttention\r\n\r\nclass ThreeLayerMLP(nn.Module):\r\n    \"\"\"A 3-layer MLP with normalization and dropout.\"\"\"\r\n\r\n    def __init__(self, dim, out_dim):\r\n        super().__init__()\r\n        self.net = nn.Sequential(\r\n            nn.Conv1d(dim, dim, 1, bias=False),\r\n            nn.BatchNorm1d(dim),\r\n            nn.ReLU(),\r\n            nn.Dropout(0.3),\r\n            nn.Conv1d(dim, dim, 1, bias=False),\r\n            nn.BatchNorm1d(dim),\r\n            nn.ReLU(),\r\n            nn.Dropout(0.3),\r\n            nn.Conv1d(dim, out_dim, 1)\r\n        )\r\n\r\n    def forward(self, x):\r\n        \"\"\"Forward pass, x can be (B, dim, N).\"\"\"\r\n        return self.net(x)\r\n\r\nclass CrossAttentionLayer(nn.Module):\r\n\r\n    def __init__(self, d_model=256, nhead=8, dropout=0.0):\r\n        super().__init__()\r\n        self.attn = MultiheadAttention(d_model, nhead, dropout=dropout, batch_first=True)\r\n        self.norm = nn.LayerNorm(d_model)\r\n        self.dropout = nn.Dropout(dropout)\r\n        self._reset_parameters()\r\n        self.nhead = nhead\r\n\r\n    def _reset_parameters(self):\r\n        for p in self.parameters():\r\n            if p.dim() > 1:\r\n                nn.init.xavier_uniform_(p)\r\n\r\n    def with_pos_embed(self, tensor, pos):\r\n        return tensor if pos is None else tensor + pos\r\n\r\n    def forward(self, source, query, batch_mask=None, attn_mask=None, pe=None, att_weights=None):\r\n        \"\"\"\r\n        source (B, N_p, d_model)\r\n        batch_offsets Tensor (b, n_p)\r\n        query Tensor (b, n_q, d_model)\r\n        attn_masks Tensor (b, n_q, n_p)\r\n        \"\"\"\r\n        B = query.shape[0]\r\n        query = self.with_pos_embed(query, pe)\r\n        k = v = source\r\n        if attn_mask is not None:\r\n            attn_mask = attn_mask.unsqueeze(1).repeat(1, self.nhead, 1, 1).view(B*self.nhead, query.shape[1], k.shape[1])\r\n            output, output_weight, src_weight = self.attn(query, k, v, key_padding_mask=batch_mask, attn_mask=attn_mask, att_weights =att_weights)  # (1, 100, d_model)\r\n        else:\r\n            output, output_weight, src_weight = self.attn(query, k, v, key_padding_mask=batch_mask, att_weights =att_weights)\r\n        self.dropout(output)\r\n        output = output + query\r\n        self.norm(output)\r\n\r\n        return output, output_weight, src_weight # (b, n_q, d_model), (b, n_q, n_v)\r\n\r\nclass SelfAttentionLayer(nn.Module):\r\n\r\n    def __init__(self, d_model=256, nhead=8, dropout=0.0, glu = False):\r\n        super().__init__()\r\n        self.attn = MultiheadAttention(\r\n            d_model,\r\n            nhead,\r\n            dropout=dropout,\r\n            batch_first=True,\r\n        )\r\n        self.nhead = nhead\r\n        self.norm = nn.LayerNorm(d_model)\r\n        self.dropout = nn.Dropout(dropout)\r\n        self.glu = glu\r\n        if glu:\r\n            self.glu_p = nn.Linear(d_model, d_model)\r\n            self.glu_g = nn.Linear(d_model, d_model)\r\n\r\n    def with_pos_embed(self, tensor, pos):\r\n        return tensor if pos is None else tensor + pos\r\n\r\n    def forward(self, x, x_mask=None, attn_mask=None, pe=None, norm=True, att_weights=None):\r\n        \"\"\"\r\n        x Tensor (b, n_w, c)\r\n        x_mask Tensor (b, n_w)\r\n        \"\"\"\r\n        B = x.shape[0]\r\n        q = k = self.with_pos_embed(x, pe)\r\n        if attn_mask is not None:\r\n            attn_mask = attn_mask.unsqueeze(1).repeat(1, self.nhead, 1, 1).view(B*self.nhead, q.shape[1], k.shape[1])\r\n            output, output_weight, src_weight = self.attn(q, k, x, key_padding_mask=x_mask, attn_mask=attn_mask, att_weights =att_weights)  # (1, 100, d_model)\r\n        else:\r\n            output, output_weight, src_weight = self.attn(q, k, x, key_padding_mask=x_mask, att_weights =att_weights)\r\n        if self.glu:\r\n            output = self.glu_p(output) * (self.glu_g(output).sigmoid())\r\n        output = self.dropout(output) + x\r\n        if norm: output = self.norm(output)\r\n        return output\r\n\r\nclass FFN(nn.Module):\r\n\r\n    def __init__(self, d_model, hidden_dim, dropout=0.0, activation_fn='relu'):\r\n        super().__init__()\r\n        if activation_fn == 'relu':\r\n            self.net = nn.Sequential(\r\n                nn.Linear(d_model, hidden_dim),\r\n                nn.ReLU(),\r\n                nn.Dropout(dropout),\r\n                nn.Linear(hidden_dim, d_model),\r\n                nn.Dropout(dropout),\r\n            )\r\n        elif activation_fn == 'gelu':\r\n            self.net = nn.Sequential(\r\n                nn.Linear(d_model, hidden_dim),\r\n                nn.GELU(),\r\n                nn.Dropout(dropout),\r\n                nn.Linear(hidden_dim, d_model),\r\n                nn.Dropout(dropout),\r\n            )\r\n        self.norm = nn.LayerNorm(d_model)\r\n\r\n    def forward(self, x, norm=True):\r\n        output = self.net(x)\r\n        output = output + x\r\n        if norm: output = self.norm(output)\r\n        return output\r\n\r\nclass MLP(nn.Module):\r\n    \"\"\" Very simple multi-layer perceptron (also called FFN)\"\"\"\r\n\r\n    def __init__(self, input_dim, hidden_dim, output_dim, num_layers):\r\n        super().__init__()\r\n        self.num_layers = num_layers\r\n        h = [hidden_dim] * (num_layers - 1)\r\n        self.layers = nn.ModuleList(nn.Linear(n, k) for n, k in zip([input_dim] + h, h + [output_dim]))\r\n\r\n    def forward(self, x):\r\n        for i, layer in enumerate(self.layers):\r\n            x = F.relu(layer(x)) if i < self.num_layers - 1 else layer(x)\r\n        return x\r\n\r\n\r\nclass QueryCompetitionIndicator(nn.Module):\r\n    \"\"\"Predict confidence from a query and its overlapping competitors.\"\"\"\r\n\r\n    def __init__(self, d_model):\r\n        super().__init__()\r\n        self.query_norm = nn.LayerNorm(d_model)\r\n        self.evidence_norm = nn.LayerNorm(3 * d_model + 1)\r\n        self.head = nn.Sequential(\r\n            nn.Linear(3 * d_model + 1, d_model),\r\n            nn.GELU(),\r\n            nn.Linear(d_model, d_model),\r\n            nn.GELU(),\r\n            nn.Linear(d_model, 2),\r\n        )\r\n\r\n    def forward(self, query, pred_masks, batch_mask):\r\n        valid = (~batch_mask).unsqueeze(1).to(pred_masks.dtype)\r\n        probabilities = pred_masks.sigmoid() * valid\r\n        areas = probabilities.sum(-1)\r\n        intersection = torch.einsum(\r\n            'bim,bjm->bij', probabilities, probabilities\r\n        )\r\n        union = areas.unsqueeze(-1) + areas.unsqueeze(1) - intersection\r\n        overlap = intersection / union.clamp_min(1e-6)\r\n        diagonal = torch.eye(\r\n            overlap.shape[-1], dtype=torch.bool, device=overlap.device\r\n        ).unsqueeze(0)\r\n        overlap = overlap.masked_fill(diagonal, 0.0)\r\n\r\n        competition = overlap / overlap.sum(-1, keepdim=True).clamp_min(1e-6)\r\n        normalized_query = self.query_norm(query)\r\n        context = torch.einsum('bij,bjd->bid', competition, normalized_query)\r\n        max_overlap = overlap.max(-1).values.unsqueeze(-1)\r\n        evidence = torch.cat(\r\n            [\r\n                normalized_query,\r\n                context,\r\n                normalized_query - context,\r\n                max_overlap,\r\n            ],\r\n            dim=-1,\r\n        )\r\n        return self.head(self.evidence_norm(evidence))\r\n    \r\n    \r\nclass DEC(nn.Module):\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    in_channels List[int] (4,) [64,96,128,160]\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    def __init__(\r\n        self,\r\n        num_layer=6,\r\n        num_class=256,\r\n        in_channel=32,\r\n        d_model=256,\r\n        nhead=8,\r\n        hidden_dim=1024,\r\n        dropout=0.0,\r\n        activation_fn='relu',\r\n        iter_pred=False,\r\n        attn_mask=False,\r\n        sampling_module=None,\r\n        kernel='top1',\r\n        global_feat='mean',\r\n        lang_att=False,\r\n        contrastive_align_loss=False,\r\n        num_proposal_fine=512,\r\n        num_proposal_query = [128,64,32,16,8,4],\r\n        num_proposal_query_inst = [128,64,32,16,8,4]\r\n    ):\r\n        super().__init__()\r\n        self.num_layer = num_layer\r\n        self.num_class = num_class\r\n        self.d_model = d_model\r\n        self.input_proj = nn.Sequential(nn.Linear(in_channel, d_model), nn.LayerNorm(d_model), nn.ReLU())\r\n        \r\n        self.input_proj_2d = nn.Sequential(nn.Linear(1024, d_model*2),nn.ReLU(),nn.Linear(d_model*2, d_model),nn.ReLU(),nn.Linear(d_model, d_model))#clip\r\n        self.sum_norm = nn.LayerNorm(d_model)\r\n        \r\n        self.lang_att = lang_att\r\n        self.contrastive_align_loss = contrastive_align_loss\r\n\r\n        H = 768\r\n        self.lang_proj = nn.Linear(H, d_model)\r\n        self.lang_norm = nn.LayerNorm(d_model)\r\n        \r\n        if sampling_module is not None:\r\n            self.sampling_module = SamplingModule(**sampling_module)\r\n        else:\r\n            self.sampling_module = None\r\n        self.num_proposal_fine = num_proposal_fine\r\n        self.num_proposal_query = num_proposal_query\r\n        self.num_proposal_query_inst = num_proposal_query_inst\r\n        self.query_generator = nn.Sequential(nn.Linear(d_model, d_model),nn.ReLU(),nn.Linear(d_model, d_model),nn.ReLU(),nn.Linear(d_model, d_model))\r\n        \r\n        # DDI and SWA\r\n        self.qia_layers = nn.ModuleList([])\r\n        self.qia_layers_fine = nn.ModuleList([])\r\n        self.qla_layers = nn.ModuleList([])\r\n        self.qqa_layers = nn.ModuleList([])\r\n        self.qqa_ffn_layers = nn.ModuleList([])\r\n        self.qia_ffn_layers = nn.ModuleList([])\r\n        self.sem_cls_heads = nn.ModuleList([])\r\n        # self.scg = nn.ModuleList([])\r\n        self.lqg = nn.ModuleList([])\r\n        if self.lang_att:\r\n            self.lla_layers = nn.ModuleList([])\r\n            self.lia_layers = nn.ModuleList([])\r\n            self.ila_layers = nn.ModuleList([])\r\n            self.lia_ffn_layers = nn.ModuleList([])\r\n            self.ila_ffn_layers = nn.ModuleList([])\r\n        for i in range(num_layer):\r\n            self.qia_layers.append(CrossAttentionLayer(d_model, nhead, dropout))\r\n            self.qia_layers_fine.append(CrossAttentionLayer(d_model, nhead, dropout))\r\n            self.qla_layers.append(CrossAttentionLayer(d_model, nhead, dropout))\r\n            self.qqa_layers.append(SelfAttentionLayer(d_model, nhead, dropout))\r\n            self.qqa_ffn_layers.append(FFN(d_model, hidden_dim, dropout, activation_fn))\r\n            self.qia_ffn_layers.append(FFN(d_model, hidden_dim, dropout, activation_fn))\r\n            \r\n            self.sem_cls_heads.append(ThreeLayerMLP(d_model, self.num_class))\r\n            # self.scg.append(SelfAttentionLayer(d_model, nhead, dropout))\r\n            self.lqg.append(CrossAttentionLayer(d_model, nhead, dropout))\r\n\r\n            self.lla_layers.append(SelfAttentionLayer(d_model, nhead, dropout))\r\n            self.lia_layers.append(CrossAttentionLayer(d_model, nhead, dropout))\r\n            self.ila_layers.append(CrossAttentionLayer(d_model, nhead, dropout))\r\n            self.lia_ffn_layers.append(FFN(d_model, hidden_dim, dropout, activation_fn))    \r\n            self.ila_ffn_layers.append(FFN(d_model, hidden_dim, dropout, activation_fn))    \r\n        self.norm_qqa = nn.LayerNorm(d_model)\r\n\r\n        self.sem_cls_head = ThreeLayerMLP(d_model, self.num_class)\r\n\r\n        self.out_norm = nn.LayerNorm(d_model)\r\n        self.out_score = nn.Sequential(nn.Linear(d_model, d_model), nn.ReLU(), nn.Linear(d_model, 1))\r\n        self.x_mask = nn.Sequential(nn.Linear(in_channel, d_model), nn.ReLU(), nn.Linear(d_model, d_model))\r\n        \r\n        self.indi_embedding = QueryCompetitionIndicator(d_model)\r\n        self.indi_norm = nn.LayerNorm(d_model)\r\n\r\n        self.iter_pred = iter_pred\r\n        self.attn_mask = attn_mask\r\n\r\n        \r\n\r\n        # Extra layers for contrastive losses\r\n        if contrastive_align_loss:\r\n            self.contrastive_align_projection_vision = nn.Sequential(nn.Linear(d_model, d_model),nn.ReLU(),nn.Linear(d_model, d_model),nn.ReLU(),nn.Linear(d_model, 64))\r\n            self.contrastive_align_projection_text = nn.Sequential(nn.Linear(d_model, d_model),nn.ReLU(),nn.Linear(d_model, d_model),nn.ReLU(),nn.Linear(d_model, 64))         \r\n        \r\n        self.scg_head = SelfAttentionLayer(d_model, nhead, dropout=0, glu=True)\r\n        \r\n    \r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
